{"id": "EUVD-2026-82295", "enisaUuid": "617bb92e-fc0e-3bd5-9562-03e57ff84ff4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: SOF: ipc4-topology: Return error for invalid number of formats\n\nWhen the number of input or output formats is zero,\nsof_ipc4_widget_setup_comp_src() and sof_ipc4_widget_setup_comp_asrc()\nprint an error and jump to the cleanup label. At that point 'ret' is\nstill 0, because the earlier sof_ipc4_get_audio_fmt() call succeeded, so\nthe function returns success and the caller never finds out that the\nwidget setup actually failed.\n\nSet ret to -EINVAL before the goto so the error gets reported.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:12:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:06:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4992cdc4eb97981d6ea66002c5b764a6115edb0c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11e828cd6b0f283ebe9dc6b4cffd38e3321e7725"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93187", "GHSA-hmgp-9jc3-w35h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6f27bcf6-0156-3a7a-a98c-fbda47d8b172", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "21a5adffad463344e9aca6ee697f45a079cb3ef5 <4992cdc4eb97981d6ea66002c5b764a6115edb0c"}, {"id": "7d76b124-ceb1-3bdc-b6a2-c73300be2e11", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "21a5adffad463344e9aca6ee697f45a079cb3ef5 <11e828cd6b0f283ebe9dc6b4cffd38e3321e7725"}, {"id": "7eec337f-0db3-3cc0-bc7c-df376d2e3c14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8d869303-7a78-3efc-a3e8-1bd1c95c89fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c13605dd-1651-38a9-bbe3-e4e89082eb39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.2"}, {"id": "db9e694e-429c-33dd-9b07-939b51da9865", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_vers